<p>
  Zippiker keeps your customers, sales and books in one place. Everything lives in a <strong>workspace</strong>: your company's private space that you share with your team.
</p>

<h2>1. Tell us about your company</h2>
<p>
  Open <.link navigate="/settings/company">Settings → Company details</.link>
  and fill in your legal name, tax ID, address and bank details (the invoice footer is a good place
  for them). These appear on every quote and invoice you print.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Payment terms</strong> decide the due date of new invoices (30 days by default).
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Number prefixes</strong>
    shape your document numbers, e.g. <code>INV-2026-0001</code>. Numbers never skip and restart every year.
  </li>
  <li>
    Operate more than one company? Add a <strong>legal entity</strong>
    for each; every document says which one issued it.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Invite your team</h2>
<p>
  In <.link navigate="/settings/workspace">Settings → Workspace</.link>, type a colleague's email and pick a role.
  They get an email with a link; once they sign up (or sign in) they land in your workspace.
  See <.link navigate="/help/team-and-billing">Team, roles &amp; billing</.link>
  for what each role can do.
</p>

<h2>3. Find your way around</h2>
<p>
  The sidebar lists the modules. Open one and its pages appear as tabs across the top: for example
  <em>Sales</em>
  has Quotes, Orders, Delivery notes, Invoices and Products.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dashboard</strong> — today's agenda, pipeline health and money owed to you.</li>
  <li><strong>Leads, Deals, Tasks</strong> — your sales pipeline (CRM).</li>
  <li><strong>Contacts, Companies</strong> — everyone you do business with.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales</strong> — quotes, orders, invoices and payments.</li>
  <li><strong>Purchasing</strong> — purchase orders to suppliers and their bills.</li>
  <li><strong>Inventory</strong> — stock on hand, movements and warehouses.</li>
  <li><strong>People</strong> — employees, leave, org chart and departments.</li>
  <li><strong>Accounting</strong> — your books, expenses and financial reports.</li>
  <li><strong>Settings</strong> — company details, custom fields, taxes, team and billing.</li>
</ul>
<.callout>
  Don't see a section? Your plan may not include that module. Workspace admins can check under <.link navigate="/settings/billing">Plan &amp; billing</.link>.
</.callout>

<h2>4. Several workspaces</h2>
<p>
  Click your workspace name at the top of the sidebar to switch between workspaces you belong to,
  or to create a new one (for a second business, for example). Each workspace has its own data,
  team and plan.
</p>

<h2>5. Make it yours</h2>
<p>
  Use the switch at the bottom of the sidebar for light, dark or automatic theme. Add
  <.link navigate="/help/custom-fields">custom fields</.link>
  to record anything Zippiker doesn't track out of the box.
</p>
